        "text": "Traders may also use moving average crossovers as buy or sell signals. For example, if the 100 day simple moving average crosses below the 200 day simple moving average, it may be considered a sell signal. The last indicator is Bollinger bands, a measure of the volatility of the market. It can also be used as an indicator of overbought or oversold conditions. Bollinger bands are made up of three a simple moving average, which is the middle band, and an upper and lower band. The settings may vary, but typically the upper and lower bands are two standard deviations away from the middle band. As volatility increases and decreases, the distance between the bands increases and decreases as well.",
        "start": 400,
        "end": 39690,
